            "review_title": "Review at Seoul Garden",
            "review_text": "Du_Ma\nNha Trang, Vietnam90 contributions\n0\nDinner\nMar 2019 • Friends\nWhy is it that in Vietnam they always turn you away at the door? \n“ sorry sir, table full” \nwhen the tables are clearly not full. \nI’ll wait ... \nAnd after the fourth time she repeated herself, I said I heard you the first time. \nWithin two minutes I was seated. \nOnce you do get seated the service and the food are excellent. \n\nI’ll never understand why restaurants always turn people around. Nobody will wait a minute?\n\nYou wonder why the poverty rate is so high but people are just incredibly lazy in this country. They don’t even try to get your business, they just turn you away and or shake their hand at you. \n\nIf you’ve been anywhere in this country you know what I mean, The Vietnamese handshake, the answer to everything.\nRead more\nWritten March 10, 2019",
